# BatchIt CLI Rules

## Schema-First Development Rules

1. All operations must be schema-defined:
   - Use Zod for schema definitions
   - Place schemas in appropriate schema files under src/schemas/
   - Include TypeScript types derived from schemas
   - Maintain clear schema documentation

2. Schema Validation Requirements:
   - All input must be validated against schemas
   - Use safeParse for validation with clear error messages
   - Include examples in schema documentation
   - Test schema validation thoroughly

3. Capability Implementation Rules:
   - Each capability must be self-contained
   - Implement standard capability interface
   - Include schema definitions for capability
   - Provide comprehensive testing

## File Organization

1. Schema Files:
   - src/schemas/core.ts: Core type definitions
   - src/schemas/filesystem.ts: Filesystem schemas
   - src/schemas/memory-bank.ts: Memory bank schemas
   - Each schema file must export its types

2. Sub-Operation Structure:
   - src/subops/index.ts: Registry and interface definitions
   - src/subops/{operation}SubOp.ts: Individual operation implementations
   - Each sub-op must follow standard interface with name, schema, description, handler
   - All sub-ops must be exported in index.ts array

3. Capability Structure:
   - src/capabilities/{name}/index.ts: Main implementation
   - src/capabilities/{name}/schema.ts: Capability schemas
   - src/capabilities/{name}/types.ts: Type definitions
   - src/capabilities/{name}/docs.ts: Documentation

4. Test Organization:
   - tests/schemas/: Schema validation tests
   - tests/capabilities/: Capability tests
   - Each test file mirrors source structure

## Coding Patterns

1. Sub-Operation Implementation:
   - Follow SubOp interface definition
   - Import schemas from appropriate source
   - Provide clear operation description
   - Implement type-safe handler
   - Use proper error handling
   - Follow naming convention: {operation}SubOp
   - Register in localFsSubOps array

2. Error Handling:
   - Use BatchError for all errors
   - Include error code and details
   - Provide clear error messages
   - Add examples to error documentation

3. Validation:
   - Use Zod schemas for validation
   - Implement safeParse for all inputs
   - Include validation in capability methods
   - Maintain clear validation errors

4. Documentation:
   - Include JSDoc comments
   - Provide usage examples
   - Document schema structures
   - Maintain capability documentation

## Testing Requirements

1. Schema Tests:
   - Test all schema validations
   - Include edge cases
   - Test error messages
   - Verify type inference

2. Capability Tests:
   - Test capability registration
   - Verify operation execution
   - Test error conditions
   - Check resource cleanup

3. Integration Tests:
   - Test capability interactions
   - Verify batch operations
   - Test error propagation
   - Check performance metrics

## Development Workflow

1. Schema Development:
   - Define schema first
   - Add validation tests
   - Implement runtime validation
   - Document schema usage

2. Capability Development:
   - Create capability interface
   - Implement schema validation
   - Add capability tests
   - Document capability usage

3. Integration:
   - Register capabilities
   - Implement batch operations
   - Add integration tests
   - Update documentation

## Code Style

1. TypeScript Usage:
   - Use strict type checking
   - Leverage type inference
   - Document complex types
   - Maintain type safety

2. Error Messages:
   - Clear and actionable
   - Include context details
   - Reference documentation
   - Provide examples

3. Documentation Style:
   - Clear and concise
   - Include examples
   - Document edge cases
   - Maintain consistency

## Performance Guidelines

1. Validation Performance:
   - Optimize schema validation
   - Cache validation results
   - Monitor validation time
   - Profile performance

2. Capability Performance:
   - Efficient resource usage
   - Smart capability loading
   - Monitor execution time
   - Implement cleanup

3. Batch Operation Performance:
   - Optimize concurrent execution
   - Manage resource usage
   - Monitor operation timing
   - Implement timeouts

## Security Requirements

1. Input Validation:
   - Validate all inputs
   - Sanitize data
   - Check permissions
   - Verify capabilities

2. Error Safety:
   - Safe error messages
   - Secure error details
   - Clean error stacks
   - Log security events

3. Resource Security:
   - Validate paths
   - Check permissions
   - Clean up resources
   - Monitor access
